Problem 1: Plus One





  🧩 Problem Statement:


You are given a large integer represented as an array of digits, where each digits[i] is a digit of the integer. Add one to the integer and return the result as an array.
Question Link
Approach:



Start from the last digit.
If the digit is less than 9, just add 1 and return.
If the digit is 9, it becomes 0 (carry over).
If all digits are 9, insert a 1 at the beginning (e.g., [9,9,9] → [1,0,0,0]).
Time Complexity: O(n) — Might loop through all digits.
Space Complexity: O(1) — In-place, except final carry using unshift.
/**
 * @param {number[]} digits
 * @return {number[]}
 */

var plusOne = function(digits) {
    for (let i = digits.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        if (digits[i] < 9) {
